<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable> Early the following morning, on the 25th of December, exactly 283 days after she met the three great Sages, the virgin Sarah gave birth to a healthy 3.9 kg male child and promptly named him Richard-Dawkins Jacobson-Shakti or Richard-Dawkins for short or Richard for shorter. The name would not be shortened any further as Sarah did not like Dick. Kathy had never before seen a birth so quick and silent. So speedily did Richard shoot out Kathy\'92s patches had hardly anytime to kick-in and she managed to get through the delivery completely sober. Something that surprised all. \
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Sarah had not known what to expect, except pain, but she felt hardly a twinge of discomfort and passed the child into the world with ease. Quite remarkably, Sarah\'92s body returned to a pre-pregnancy state within hours. Her skin, musculature and internal tissue tissue were perfectly elastic and any subsequent medical examination would conclude she had never given birth and was, in fact, virgo-intacto. The unwanted presence of Alexander Shakti in the birthing room, bothered her greatly, but it was infinitely preferable to Eloise Shakti\'92s presence under the pretence of support. She didn\'92t want her husband to see her exposed flesh and insisted he stand by her head and hold her hand. Even when she had \'91consummated\'92 their relationship, she recalled with disgust, it had been in total darkness.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>The visit to her private suite by the High Elvis and the remaining two great Sages was a highlight. Solo and Chilo were expecting Sarah would still harbour some significant anger towards them, but were surprised by her welcome.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93What is this?\'94 Sarah smiled with delight at the boy in her arms. \'93Look Richard, the men who are responsible for your birth.\'94 \
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93The One-after-the-One!\'94 The High Elvis proudly announced as he, Solo and Chilo bent to their knees and bowed in reverence. \'93To be alive in the time of the Saviour is truly an honour.\'94 He offered up a three small gifts.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93Are you three what passes for wise men these days? \'94 Sarah giggled and brought each gift to her ear before giving them a little shake. \'93Let me guess Frankincense? Myrrh?\'94\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93Praise be to the Dawkins.\'94 Solo and Chilo were never out of character. \
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93Well if you can keep this a secret for a while I would be very grateful.\'94 Sarah didn\'92t need a stampede of Elvi in her room. \
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93Are we forgiven Blessed Mother?\'94 Solo asked, quietly expecting rejection. \
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93Richard is the best thing that has ever happened to me! You are forgiven.\'94 Sarah could not believe she was forgiving the unforgivable, but the wonder of her son rendered her euphoric. \
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93We will have to make an official announcement to the Elvi, but I am also concerned about the security implications.\'94 The High Elvis brought down the mood. \'93He is our Saviour and must be protected at all costs.\'94\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93Labeling him Saviour will probably draw unwanted attention.\'94 Sarah returned fire. \'93We are talking about danger from the elites of the dominion are we not? My people do not tolerate hope. If they do not know his name, they cannot target him. Although I think it will be impossible to hide his existence, the Elvi will surely notice that I am not pregnant. Can all the Elvi keep a secret?\'94\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93They will have to. The safety of the One-after-the-One is paramount. You will have 24 hour Elvi protection. I will not take no for an answer.\'94\

